  "description": "Guardrails as versioned YAML or JSON rule files for C# and .NET model calls, agent tools and data operations. Evaluate allow and deny lists, patterns, ranges, JSON Schema checks and operation limits in your process, with no model call during rule evaluation. A deny wins over an allow; an invalid rule-file edit keeps the last good version. Decisions identify the rule set, document and version. An AI edit to a rule file is validated and then takes effect by default; access-widening edits are flagged so your own edit writer can hold them for approval. Optional compilation of plain-language rules into deterministic checks is experimental and opt-in. Add this package to IntentSharp when rule sets live in files. Your application must integrate and honor the checkpoint decisions; this is not a sandbox for arbitrary application code. Commercial software, not open source: evaluate free for 30 days on development and test systems; after that, business use needs a paid license, and production use needs one from the first day (intentsharp.com/pricing).",
